{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>When HaShem your Elohim expands your border</b>, the sense of this expansion is not like that which He says (Deuteronomy 19:8–9), 'And if HaShem your Elohim expands your border,' and so forth, 'you shall add three more cities for yourself besides these three,' for if so, flesh of desire would not be permitted when they enter the Land. But there (Deuteronomy 19:1) it is said, 'When HaShem your Elohem cuts off the nations whose land HaShem your Elohim is giving you' — and these are the seven nations that He mentions everywhere — and then He set apart three cities, and so Joshua did (Joshua 20). Afterward He said, 'When HaShem your Elohim expands your border, as He swore to your fathers' — and this alludes to the ten nations that were given to Abraham. But here He says, <b>as He spoke to you</b>, and these are these nations whose land HaShem your Elohim is giving you, for immediately after they conquered and divided the Land, flesh of desire was permitted to them. And the phrase <b>when the place is far from you</b> does not mean that it becomes permitted only by distance of the place alone, for if so, the inhabitants of Jerusalem would be forbidden in flesh of desire. Rather, He speaks to all Israel and says to them: when HaShem expands your border and you are not all of you dwelling around the Mishkan as you are today in the wilderness, the flesh of ordinary slaughter (חולין) will be permitted to you, for it is impossible that you should all go from a distant place to the place that HaShem will choose and slaughter peace-offerings for everything you eat:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "The Hebrew abbreviation א\"א has been resolved as אי אפשר ('it is impossible'), which fits the context; it could theoretically also stand for איש אחד, but that does not yield a coherent reading here."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:48:43.870129123Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}